Z||000000||Jncomutt||06-04-2001||09:33 PM||||Hi, I was wondering if anyone knew where I can buy/order the air scoops that mount to the trunk vents and come over the middle of the car.  I've looked around but couldn't find em anywhere.  <P>I'm not talking about the indy scoop that sits in the middle.  I found that if anyone else is interested.  Its listed here for only $189!  Its a fiberglass part and fairly inexpensive I think for what it is.   <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A> <P>Below is a picture of the kind of scoops I'm trying to find:  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Mods/daytona8.jpg">  <P>Thanks again!<P><p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||qwikgta||06-04-2001||09:50 PM||||Don't take this the wrong way but you do realize that the reason for the vents is to vent hot air out, not suck cold air in.  If its for show only than thats cool, some people drive the car that way and they could have overheating probs.  If you want to add cold air into the engine then you should do the side scoops.  I'm sure that some will disagree.   Just my $.02<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||06-04-2001||09:59 PM||||My plan is to only use the driver side scoop.  I want to seal it to the flat cover that came on my 84.  Inside I will have funnel shape that will be connected to the intake hose goin to the TBI.  Thus making a "ram-Air" sort of thing.<P>I don't know much of aerodynamics, haven't even takin class on that yet in this highschool.  What I do know is that there is a slip stream that prevents the side scoops from workin too well.  I was thinkin the vents over the roof will catch more air.<P>As far as heating, I will still have the vent in the center (its an 84) and the right side vent cover (taken from my 86) to help in cooling.<P>Any ideas to this??<P>------------------<BR>17 year old Fierophile<BR>'86 Coupe 160k miles<BR>'84 Mint Beauty 51k and original tires!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||06-04-2001||10:23 PM||||IRM use to make them. They were called Fi-Air-O scoops. IRM doesn't make them anymore. I have not heard of anyone else making them.<BR>FOCOA has a scoop called a "Lazy-C" which wraps around the sail panel on a notchback. I am not sure how much air it would catch since it sits against the edge of the panel.<BR>For "over-the-roof" type cooling aside from the 2 above and the Indy style scoop, The only one left is the Harwood Scoop but that is very large. (it's like the big scoop on the Indy/F1 type of cars.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||sjp777||06-04-2001||11:22 PM||||Dammit! That driver's side scoop in the picture is exactly what I'm looking for, but seems non-existant to buy. I don't think the one posted as a link in that post is the side one. From the drawing it looks like another center scoop.<P>Does ANYONE know where to get the driver's side full over the roof scoop?!<P>And Jncomutt don't even think about stealing my idea for a sealed scoop directly into a flat K&N filter into a duct leading directly into the throttle body.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg">  <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A><p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_24||06-04-2001||11:45 PM||||There is a place in the Big Fiero Parts book that has a place that sells those scoops.  I am not sure if they still do.  If you are doing it for show go for it.  But if you are going to do daily driving watch out for over heating.  Fiero's are what you call a belly breather.  Warm air rises and goes out the vents.  You will overheat and loose a lot of performance on the car with those style scoops.  If you are looking to cool the engine go with the Indy scoop.  <P>Craig<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 06-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||sjp777||06-05-2001||12:03 AM||||Did you not read the concept above?<P>It's right there, and it ain't about cooling. Jeez||||reg||1
