Z||000008||grinthock||06-05-2001||11:03 PM||||I DID read the about topic, and I will now voice my opinion.... The air in the fiero is sucked in from the bottom and flows out and BACK through the vents --- quite efficient!  If you put those there you are FIGHTING the air that is trying to LEAVE...  RAM air effect could be kinda tough because of this... The side scoop thing is better, and contrary to your beleif the side scoops DO make a difference the fieroshop here in Canada did a dyno test to prove....   The FieroShop here in Canada has a over the roof scoop, but it's for a intercooler.... Other than that, they do'nt serve much of a purpose||||reg||1
