Z||000012||Jncomutt||06-05-2001||11:22 PM||||Thanks for the replies everyone, I didn't really know all the technical stuff about the cooling.<P>Thing is, I'm not looking for engine compartment cooling.  I want just the driver side, so it can be sealed down to the flat 84 cover, and funneled into the tube, leading to my k&n, and holley big bore throttle body.  I will still have the middle vent open, and an 86 vent on the pass. side.  If cooling becomes a problem even with only 1 "over the roof" scoop, I can always resort to the Big side scoops on both sides which I was told are Very Effective.<P>I think its just SJP777 and I are the only ones glorifing the results.  Considering we both seem to have the same exact idea, lol.  I'm going to contact IRM if I can somehow, or someone who has had one, see if I can make a mold of it perhaps so I can fiberglass it myself.  I've never done any work with fiberglass or any body work in fact.  But, looks like I may have to start.<P>Oh yea, and SJP777, good luck on your exploration of this idea.<P>------------------<BR>17 year old Fierophile<BR>'86 Coupe 160k miles<BR>'84 Mint Beauty 51k and original tires!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Seanh||06-05-2001||11:34 PM||||I think thats a pretty good idea ya go goin' there. I was thinking about doing somthing like that a while back, but useing a 1/4 window scoop. I highly doubt you would have any overheating problems with doing this. I mean Iv ran my 86GT for about 40 minutes with the vent completly blocked off, and still didn't have any problems. Keep us posted about the outcome if you call IRM about it.||||reg||1
